    # rax=index of next `use `/`use:` line's 'u' (after indent), or -1.
    # SWAR 8-byte newline skip between line starts (the byte loop walked
    # ~5 instr/byte); the `use `/`use:` check is one dword compare each.
    # All loads stay inside [st,lim) so no NUL overread is possible.
    # Volatile-only leaf; assembled+diff-verified in scripts/swar_twins.s
    # (550k randomized differential cases vs the byte-loop reference).
